# Objective

Create a secure development environment for the new homepage before its official deployment.

The primary objective was to prevent accidental indexing of the development version by search engines while allowing access only to authorized users.

Planned security architecture:

```text
Browser
        ↓
HTTP Basic Authentication
        ↓
.htaccess
        ↓
.htpasswd
        ↓
Authorized access only
        ↓
index.php
```

---

# Completed Tasks

## 1. Risk Assessment

A review of possible approaches to protect the development version was carried out.

The following methods were evaluated:

- robots.txt
- Meta Robots
- X-Robots-Tag
- Apache password protection

The analysis concluded that HTTP Basic Authentication provides the most reliable protection for a development environment.

---

## 2. Creating the .htaccess File

A dedicated configuration file was created:

```text
.htaccess
```

The following features were implemented:

- HTTP Basic Authentication;
- directory listing disabled;
- search engine indexing restricted through HTTP headers.

Architecture:

```text
Apache
        ↓
.htaccess
        ↓
User authentication
        ↓
Access granted
```

---

## 3. Creating the .htpasswd File

A secure password file was created:

```text
.htpasswd
```

Completed actions:

- generation of a bcrypt password hash;
- administrator credentials configured;
- secure storage of the password file.

Workflow:

```text
Username
        ↓
Password
        ↓
bcrypt
        ↓
.htpasswd
```

---

## 4. Configuring HTTP Basic Authentication

Apache's built-in authentication system was configured.

Verified functionality:

- browser login dialog appears;
- username and password validation works correctly;
- unauthorized access is blocked.

Authentication flow:

```text
Page request
        ↓
Apache
        ↓
401 Unauthorized
        ↓
Login dialog
        ↓
.htpasswd verification
        ↓
Website access
```

---

## 5. Verifying bcrypt Compatibility

Apache compatibility with modern password hashing was tested.

Hash format:

```text
bcrypt ($2y$)
```

Testing confirmed that the hosting environment successfully supports bcrypt without requiring the legacy APR1 format.

---

## 6. Configuring X-Robots-Tag

The following HTTP response header was added:

```text
X-Robots-Tag:
noindex,
nofollow,
noarchive,
nosnippet,
noimageindex
```

This instructs search engines not to index the development version.

---

## 7. Adding the Meta Robots Tag

The following tag was inserted into:

```text
index.php
```

```html
<meta name="robots"
content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex">
```

This provides an additional HTML-level restriction for search engine crawlers.

---

## 8. Verifying the Security Architecture

The complete protection workflow was tested.

Final architecture:

```text
Browser
        ↓
HTTP Basic Authentication
        ↓
.htaccess
        ↓
.htpasswd
        ↓
index.php
        ↓
<meta name="robots">
        ↓
Rendered page
```

---

## 9. Final Testing

The following items were verified:

- authentication dialog;
